    "result_text": "The change is complete and verified. Both acceptance tests pass with a clean build/start/test/stop cycle.\n\n## What I built\n\nA full-stack **Projects** feature \u2014 track projects you do for clients, each showing the client's name \u2014 added entirely as new files following the app's additive conventions.\n\n**Database** (`V3__projects.sql`): new `project` table with `id`, `name`, and a `client_id` FK to `client`.\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor REST, all new classes + one YAML per endpoint):\n- `GET /api/projects` (`ProjectsGet`) \u2014 lists projects oldest-first, joining each against `client` to include the client's **name** (`ProjectView`), so the UI never shows a raw id.\n- `POST /api/projects` (`ProjectsPost`) \u2014 validates the name and that the client exists, saves, records a `PROJECT_CREATED` audit entry, and returns the created row with its client name.\n- `Project` entity, `ProjectRepository`, `NewProject` request body, `ProjectView` DTO.\n\n**Test seed support** (`TestSupportController`, the schema-evolving seed path): `reset` now truncates `project` (with referential integrity dropped around both truncates so the FK-referenced `client` clears too), and `seed` inserts `projects` rows by explicit fixture ids.\n\n**Front-end** (three new files):\n- `routes/projects.index.tsx` \u2014 the `/projects` page (route tree regenerates from the directory).\n- `features/projects/nav.slot.tsx` \u2014 the `nav-projects` link, filling the `app.nav` slot.\n- `features/projects/ProjectsPage.tsx` \u2014 a form (`project-form-name`, `project-form-client` select whose option values are client ids, `project-form-submit`) and a `projects-table` with `project-row-{id}` rows showing `project-name` and `project-client` (the client's name). It reads projects under the `['projects']` query key and the client select options under the shared `['clients']` key, creating via `useMutation` + `invalidateQueries`.\n\nAll `data-testid` anchors match the spec exactly, and no pinned scaffolding was touched.",
